{
  "format": "supersilvia-workspace",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Fold",
  "kind": "solids",
  "blurb": "A box folded like a kaleidoscope into a fractal of its own copies",
  "layout": "linear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "slug": "note",
      "pos": {
        "x": 40.0,
        "y": 40.0
      },
      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Fold mirrors space onto one wedge of a symmetry, turns it and scales it, Iterations times, then puts the box in the folded space: a fractal of its copies for the price of one box. An Oscillator swings Turn X either side of 0, so the fractal twists and folds back each loop. Try Scale between 1.5 and 3, Iterations, and the Symmetry on Cube with Scale 3 for a sponge."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
